  "notes": "Transcribed 2026-11-11 from the official Southern Utah University 2026-2027 General Catalog (current edition, catoid=28) Business Education program page and its linked official degree map, 'Business Education Degree Maps (2026-2027)', 'Business Education (Campus)' tab, last updated/reviewed July 27, 2026. Semester placement is the university's official sample 4-year campus academic plan (SUU Program Maps, 2026-2027), which the source itself labels a guide only; students confirm specifics in Degree Works with a Student Success Advisor. Collected as the BS: the program is a combined BA/BS, the catalog prints Total Credits, BA Degree: 121 and Total Credits, BS Degree: 120 as separate lines, and the map totals exactly the BS figure of 120; the map expressly states that students electing the BA take 16 credits of one foreign language, which are not included in the map. No 'with Licensure' degree-total line is printed on this catalog page (unlike the held SUU education programs, where a separate licensure total conflicts with the map); the catalog footnote states that students who complete their teaching methods course(s) and student teaching as part of their major requirements will have those credits counted toward their licensure requirements, and that students completing the degree without licensure will need additional coursework to meet the 120-credit minimum. Every term's courses sum to the map's printed term total (16/16/15/15/15/16/15/12) and the plan to 120. DISCLOSED map/catalog differences, recorded on the catalog side where the catalog prints a specific code: the map prints CSCY 2100 for Spreadsheet Applications where the catalog's Business Information Technology Core lists BA 2010 - Spreadsheet Applications (BA 2010 recorded); the map prints SPED 2030 for Educating Exceptional Students where the catalog's Pre-Admission Courses list SPED 2010 - Educating Exceptional Students (SPED 2010 recorded). The map's BE 4900, BE 4950 and BE 4980 are the program-specific methods and student-teaching courses the catalog lists generically as 'Academic 3900/4900 - Methods Course(s)' (2-3 credits) and 'Academic 4980 - Student Teaching' (9 credits); BE 4980 is recorded at the catalog's 9 credits, and the two BE methods courses together exceed the catalog's generic 2-3 credit methods line, so the map's education/licensure courses total more than the catalog's generic Professional Education Requirements heading of 36-37 credits (whose Pre-Admission Courses block is itself headed 18-19 credits while its listed courses sum to 18-20); the degree total and every map term reconcile exactly at 120, so the plan is recorded at 120 with these heading differences disclosed (Rotor-Wing/Biomedical header-error precedent). COMM 1070 in Spring Year 1 is the map's exercise of the Business Information Technology Core's 'Complete One of the Following' choice (ART 2210 - Digital Tools or COMM 1070 - Introduction to Visual Communication Graphics). Catalog titles are recorded where the map shortens them. The catalog also requires a keyboarding test or course and the Business PRAXIS test, neither printed with credits; neither is a course slot in this plan.",
